{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And Yosef harnessed his chariot.</b> He himself harnessed the horses to the chariot, to hasten for the honor of his father." "<b>And he appeared to him.</b> Yosef appeared to his father." "<b>And he wept upon his neck a good while.</b> An expression of multiplying weeping — and likewise ״כִּי לֹא עַל אִישׁ יָשִׂים עוֹד״ (Job 34) is an expression of multiplicity: He does not lay additional charges upon him beyond his sin; so too here, he multiplied and added in weeping more than usual. But Yaakov did not fall upon Yosef's neck and did not kiss him — and our Rabbis said: he was reciting Shema."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:44.245832948Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}